From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:37:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: opp: allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points: Add
 the A733

The A733 picks the voltage and frequency set of each CPU operating
point by a speed bin that its eFuse holds, the same way the A100, H6
and H616 do. Add its compatible string to the binding.

The speed bin is the fuse value, and the A733 has bins 20 and 21. Allow
more than one digit in the opp-microvolt-speed<N> property names.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the OPP table with this
compatible is found, and the cpufreq driver binds to it and creates the
policies of both clusters.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml     | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml
index 75ab552f6ecd..96f67697fd97 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ properties:
       - allwinner,sun50i-a100-operating-points
       - allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points
       - allwinner,sun50i-h616-operating-points
+      - allwinner,sun60i-a733-operating-points
 
   nvmem-cells:
     description: |
@@ -56,7 +57,7 @@ patternProperties:
           bit per speed bin index.
 
     patternProperties:
-      "^opp-microvolt-speed[0-9]$": true
+      "^opp-microvolt-speed[0-9]+$": true
 
     required:
       - opp-hz
